{"availability":"available","full":"clauderic/react-sortable-hoc","name":"react-sortable-hoc","description":"A set of higher-order components to turn any list into an animated, accessible and touch-friendly sortable list✌️","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":10884,"forks":959,"created":"2016-06-08T03:11:35Z","updated":"2023-09-13T09:49:18Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://clauderic.github.io/react-sortable-hoc/","topics":["drag-and-drop","dragging","front-end","grid","higher-order-component","javascript","react","sortable","sorting"],"demo":"https://clauderic.github.io/react-sortable-hoc/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:27.375Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:27.375Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:27.375Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T13:03:27.375Z","stars":10884,"forks":959}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Warning This library is no longer actively maintained. It will continue to receive critical security updates, but there are no new features planned. In future versions of React, the findDOMNode method will be deprecated. This method is a critical piece of the architecture of react-sortable-hoc, and the library will stop working in the future when that method is removed from react-dom. All development efforts have been redirected towards @dnd-kit. It provides feature parity, built with a modern and extensible architecture, supports complex use-cases and has accessibility features built-in. New…","There are already a number of great Drag & Drop libraries out there (for instance, react-dnd is fantastic). If those libraries fit your needs, you should definitely give them a try first. However, most of those libraries rely on the HTML5 Drag & Drop API, which has some severe limitations. For instance, things rapidly become tricky if you need to support touch devices, if you need to lock dragging to an axis, or want to animate the nodes as they're being sorted. React Sortable HOC aims to provide a simple set of higher-order components to fill those gaps. If you're looking for a dead-simple,…"],"features":["Higher Order Components – Integrates with your existing components","Drag handle, auto-scrolling, locked axis, events, and more!","Suuuper smooth animations – Chasing the 60FPS dream 🌈","Works with virtualization libraries: react-virtualized, react-tiny-virtual-list, react-infinite, etc.","Horizontal lists, vertical lists, or a grid ↔ ↕ ⤡"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/clauderic/react-sortable-hoc/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"80089cf9f1de43f9cdba6ed01bf80c05daf7a7a9f73363a7fa745e5bb3e3b08f","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:27.447Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:27.447Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Warning This library is no longer actively maintained. It will continue to receive critical security updates, but there are no new features planned. In future versions of React, the findDOMNode method will be deprecated. This method is a critical piece of the architecture of react-sortable-hoc, and the library will stop working in the future when that method is removed from react-dom. All development efforts have been redirected towards @dnd-kit. It provides feature parity, built with a modern and extensible architecture, supports complex use-cases and has accessibility features built-in. New…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/clauderic/react-sortable-hoc/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"80089cf9f1de43f9cdba6ed01bf80c05daf7a7a9f73363a7fa745e5bb3e3b08f","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/clauderic/react-sortable-hoc/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:27.447Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2023-09-13T09:49:18Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/clauderic/react-sortable-hoc/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T13:03:27.448Z","hash":"80089cf9f1de43f9cdba6ed